 **Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
 
+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+Staff ask the veterinarian directory's question in reverse: which veterinarians hold a given specialty. A second page answers it (requested 2026-08-08). It lists every specialty the clinic knows, by its stored name, each with the veterinarians holding it `[REQ-VET-003]`. A veterinarian is named first name then last name, as in "Helen Leary". A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere on the page, which lists specialties rather than the full roster. Every specialty appears together on one page, with no paging. The page only reads: NG-2 is unchanged, so neither veterinarians nor specialties can be managed here. The page has an address of its own, and knowing that address is the only way to reach it. Nothing in the system links to it, and no navigation entry leads to it. A visible entry point is not part of this requirement.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the page is opened at its own address, then every one of them is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the page is opened, then each holder is named first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the page is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any number of specialties, when the page is opened, then all of them appear together, without paging.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the system's pages, when they are checked, then none carries a navigation entry or a link to the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A specialty held by no veterinarian still appears, with no veterinarian named under it.
+2. A clinic that knows no specialties still renders the page, listing none.
+3. Specialties, and the veterinarians within each, appear in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
